        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Taxila</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1000 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Possibly around 1000 BCE, when the first major settlement was established on the Hathial mound; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramayana">Ramayana</a> says that Bharata, the brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a>, founded it and named it for his son Taksha.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the Pothohar Plateau of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, on the eastern side of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a>, about 25 kilometres north-west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islamabad">Islamabad</a>–Rawalpindi area.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">A capital of Gandhara; surrender to Alexander in 326 BCE; the Mauryan governorship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indo-greek-kingdom">Indo-Greek</a>, Indo-Parthian and Kushan cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirkap">Sirkap</a> and Sirsukh; a centre of learning with teachers and students such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanakya">Chanakya</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panini">Pāṇini</a> and Charaka; Buddhist stupas and monasteries; devastation by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Taxila is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, and its ancient sites have been a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> since 1980.</span></div>
